  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Holistic Conservation of the World&apos;s Largest Northern White-cheeked Gibbon Population in Pu Mat National Park, Vietnam</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(1) Accurately estimate the gibbon population and map its distribution inside Pu Mat National Park, (2) Professionalize the community-based snare removal and gibbon monitoring teams, and their use of SMART (Spatial Monitoring and Reporting Tool), (3) Introduce situational crime prevention to further reduce illegal activity inside the national park, and, (4) Improve local capacity for protected area management and planning.</narrative>
  </description>
